{"id":"GHSA-mf2j-8f84-cc9q","axis":"advisories","repo":"flavorjones/loofah","sha":"2f31e7fae36036c9882d3d0fae720e1014c57cd1","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -5,6 +5,13 @@"," ### Fixed"," "," * Fix `:double_breakpoint`, which left document fragments unchanged despite its documented example. The scrubber now changes only paragraphs inside the scrubbed node, and its run time on a document grows linearly, not quadratically, with the paragraph count. #309 @OskarEichler","+### Security","+","+* Fix quadratic-time scrubbing of the `href` and `xlink:href` attributes of SVG elements. Only Ruby 3.1 and earlier are affected, because Ruby 3.2 introduced linear-time regexp matching. See [GHSA-mf2j-8f84-cc9q](https://github.com/flavorjones/loofah/security/advisories/GHSA-mf2j-8f84-cc9q). @flavorjones","+","+### Added","+","+* `Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.prefixed_attribute_name` and `Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.scrub_attribute_value` expose the html5lib attribute name and value rules, so downstream consumers can apply them instead of carrying their own copy. @flavorjones"," "," "," ## 2.25.2 / 2026-07-15"],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"lib/loofah/html5/scrub.rb","lines":["@@ -60,11 +60,7 @@ def allowed_element?(element_name)","         #  alternative implementation of the html5lib attribute scrubbing algorithm","         def scrub_attributes(node)","           node.attribute_nodes.each do |attr_node|","-            attr_name = if attr_node.namespace","-              \"#{attr_node.namespace.prefix}:#{attr_node.node_name}\"","-            else","-              attr_node.node_name","-            end","+            attr_name = prefixed_attribute_name(attr_node)"," ","             if DATA_ATTRIBUTE_NAME.match?(attr_name)","               next","@@ -75,20 +71,7 @@ def scrub_attributes(node)","               next","             end"," ","-            if SafeList::ATTR_VAL_IS_URI.include?(attr_name)","-              next if scrub_uri_attribute(attr_node)","-            end","-","-            if SafeList::SVG_ATTR_VAL_ALLOWS_REF.include?(attr_name)","-              scrub_attribute_that_allows_local_ref(attr_node)","-            end","-","-            next unless SafeList::SVG_ALLOW_LOCAL_HREF.include?(node.name) &&","-              SafeList::SVG_HREF_ATTRIBUTES.include?(attr_name) &&","-              attr_node.value =~ /^\\s*[^#\\s].*/m","-","-            attr_node.remove","-            next","+            scrub_attribute_value(node, attr_node, attr_name)","           end"," ","           scrub_css_attribute(node)","@@ -102,6 +85,39 @@ def scrub_attributes(node)","           force_correct_attribute_escaping!(node)","         end"," ","+        #  The name an attribute is matched by in the safelists, qualified by its namespace prefix.","+        def prefixed_attribute_name(attr_node)","+          if attr_node.namespace","+            \"#{attr_node.namespace.prefix}:#{attr_node.node_name}\"","+          else","+            attr_node.node_name","+          end","+        end","+","+        #  Apply the html5lib value rules to an attribute that is already permitted by name.","+        #  Returns true when `scrub_uri_attribute` removed the attribute, in which case the caller","+        #  should stop scrubbing it.","+        def scrub_attribute_value(node, attr_node, attr_name = prefixed_attribute_name(attr_node))","+          if SafeList::ATTR_VAL_IS_URI.include?(attr_name)","+            return true if scrub_uri_attribute(attr_node)","+          end","+","+          if SafeList::SVG_ATTR_VAL_ALLOWS_REF.include?(attr_name)","+            scrub_attribute_that_allows_local_ref(attr_node)","+          end","+","+          # The whitespace run is `[^\\S\\n]*` rather than `\\s*` so that it cannot cross a line","+          # boundary. With `\\s*` the engine rescanned the entire run from every line start,","+          # which is quadratic in the length of an all-whitespace value.","+          if SafeList::SVG_ALLOW_LOCAL_HREF.include?(node.name) &&","+              SafeList::SVG_HREF_ATTRIBUTES.include?(attr_name) &&","+              attr_node.value =~ /^[^\\S\\n]*[^#\\s]/","+            attr_node.remove","+          end","+","+          false","+        end","+","         def scrub_css_attribute(node)","           style = node.attributes[\"style\"]","           style.value = scrub_css(style.value) if style"],"additions":35,"deletions":19,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/html5/test_sanitizer.rb","lines":["@@ -342,6 +342,13 @@ def test_should_treat_a_malformed_data_uri_mediatype_as_text_plain","         xhtmloutput = \"<#{tag_name}></#{tag_name}>\"","         check_sanitization(input, output, xhtmloutput)","       end","+","+      define_method \"test_#{tag_name}_should_forbid_nonlocal_#{attr_name}_after_a_local_ref\" do","+        input = %(<#{tag_name} #{attr_name}=\"#foo\\nhttp://bad.com/foo\"/>)","+        output = \"<#{tag_name_dc}></#{tag_name_dc}>\"","+        xhtmloutput = \"<#{tag_name}></#{tag_name}>\"","+        check_sanitization(input, output, xhtmloutput)","+      end","     end","   end"," "],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/html5/test_scrub.rb","lines":["@@ -366,4 +366,62 @@ class UnitHTML5Scrub < Loofah::TestCase","       assert_nil(Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.send(:data_uri_mediatype, \"data:text/plain\"))","     end","   end","+","+  describe \".prefixed_attribute_name\" do","+    it \"qualifies a namespaced attribute with its prefix\" do","+      node = Loofah.html4_fragment(%(<svg><use xlink:href=\"#p\"></use></svg>)).at_css(\"use\")","+","+      assert_equal([\"xlink:href\"], node.attribute_nodes.map { |a| Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.prefixed_attribute_name(a) })","+    end","+","+    it \"uses the bare name when there is no namespace\" do","+      node = Loofah.html4_fragment(%(<a href=\"#p\"></a>)).at_css(\"a\")","+","+      assert_equal([\"href\"], node.attribute_nodes.map { |a| Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.prefixed_attribute_name(a) })","+    end","+  end","+","+  describe \".scrub_attribute_value\" do","+    it \"reports that a removed uri attribute needs no further scrubbing\" do","+      node = Loofah.html4_fragment(%(<a href=\"javascript:alert(1)\"></a>)).at_css(\"a\")","+","+      assert(Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.scrub_attribute_value(node, node.attribute_nodes.first))","+      assert_empty(node.attribute_nodes)","+    end","+","+    it \"reports that a permitted uri attribute still needs scrubbing\" do","+      node = Loofah.html4_fragment(%(<a href=\"http://example.com/\"></a>)).at_css(\"a\")","+","+      refute(Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.scrub_attribute_value(node, node.attribute_nodes.first))","+      assert_equal(\"http://example.com/\", node[\"href\"])","+    end","+","+    it \"removes an svg href that is not a local reference\" do","+      node = Loofah.html4_fragment(%(<svg><use href=\"http://bad.com/x\"></use></svg>)).at_css(\"use\")","+","+      refute(Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.scrub_attribute_value(node, node.attribute_nodes.first))","+      assert_empty(node.attribute_nodes)","+    end","+","+    it \"keeps an svg href that is a local reference\" do","+      node = Loofah.html4_fragment(%(<svg><use href=\"#p\"></use></svg>)).at_css(\"use\")","+","+      refute(Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.scrub_attribute_value(node, node.attribute_nodes.first))","+      assert_equal(\"#p\", node[\"href\"])","+    end","+  end","+","+  describe \".scrub_attributes\" do","+    it \"keeps scrubbing the remaining attributes after removing one\" do","+      fragment = Loofah.html4_fragment(%(<svg><use href=\"http://bad.com/x\" fill=\"url(http://bad.com/) #fff\"></use></svg>))","+","+      assert_equal(%(<svg><use fill=\"#fff\"></use></svg>), fragment.scrub!(:strip).to_s)","+    end","+","+    it \"keeps scrubbing the remaining attributes after a uri attribute is removed\" do","+      fragment = Loofah.html4_fragment(%(<svg><use href=\"javascript:alert(1)\" fill=\"url(http://bad.com/) #fff\"></use></svg>))","+","+      assert_equal(%(<svg><use fill=\"#fff\"></use></svg>), fragment.scrub!(:strip).to_s)","+    end","+  end"," end",""],"additions":58,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":107,"deletions":19,"truncated":false,"file_count":4},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-13T17:02:40.170286+00:00"}